#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""wf-effort-budget — emit the effort budget's option set and wording, mechanically.

The MIRROR of `wf-model-budget`, for the other half of the budget. `audit`
Step 0.4c/0.4d render the same five lanes — `analytical · Lead`, `analytical · IC`,
`creative-text`, `creative-visual`, `code` — each offering the rungs of the effort
ladder in cost order with the lane's recommended rung marked `(recommended)`. Until
now that ladder was RECONSTRUCTED from prose by the running agent on every run. The
model half of the budget was mechanised on 2026-08-20 after a re-audit read a
project's stale `## Model statics` and proposed a superseded pool; the effort half was
left on prose, which is the same hole with nothing plugging it. Reported 2026-08-26: a
session rebuilding "the budget questions" reached for a project's instantiated
`org-config.md` and reproduced the stale lane structure it found there.

FIVE LANES DO NOT FIT ONE CALL, and the grouping is not this script's to choose.
`AskUserQuestion` accepts at most FOUR objects per call (`platform.md` § header), so
the five lanes render as TWO calls with the IDENTICAL grouping the model budget uses:
CALL A carries the three structural lanes (`analytical · Lead`, `analytical · IC`,
`code`) and CALL B the two creative lanes. The two budgets render back to back and
must offer the same categories in the same order (`org-config.template.md` § The four
lanes); a caller that regroups either one by hand reintroduces the drift both scripts
exist to foreclose.

WHAT IT DERIVES, and from where. No rung, no model ID, and no sentence of question
copy is written in this file (`SKILL.md` Principle 9a — constants are stated once):

  * The ladder, in cost order most-expensive-first — parsed from
    `org-config.template.md` § Effort statics. Table order is cost order; this script
    never re-sorts.
  * The per-lane recommended rung — parsed from that section's recommendation table,
    whose canonical lane labels map onto the lane keys below.
  * PER-MODEL RUNG AVAILABILITY — parsed from `references/platform.md`, where the
    per-model claims live (facts 12b/12c: one model has no `xhigh`, one spans all
    five, one REJECTS `effort` entirely). Both facts are DOCUMENTED and unverified,
    so what they produce is an offer, never an enforcement. A model platform.md says
    nothing about is treated as supporting the whole ladder, which is fact 12b's own
    reading ("availability depending on the model") and never silently narrows a
    lane.
  * The question header and body per call — parsed from `org-config.template.md`
    § Budget question wording, the one home of that copy. This emitter prints the
    WHOLE call so the caller renders it verbatim and assembles nothing: an option set
    produced mechanically under a header retyped from memory is still half a
    hand-built question.

THE LANE'S MODEL IS AN INPUT, because the ladder depends on it. Resolution order,
highest first:
  1. `--models lane=model,...` — what the model budget just resolved. The model calls
     are questions 3 and 4 and the effort calls are 5 and 6, so a model supplied here
     is NEWER than anything a file recorded, and it wins.
  2. `--config <org-config.md>` — the recorded per-lane model on a re-audit.
  3. The lane's RECOMMENDED model, from § Model statics. A deterministic fallback
     used ONLY to compute rung availability, never emitted as a model choice: with no
     model resolved there is no ladder to window, and guessing the widest one would
     offer rungs the lane may not accept.

THE PRE-SELECTED DEFAULT is the recorded rung from `--config` on a re-audit, ELSE the
lane's recommended rung on a first run (INV-BUDGET, `audit-setup.md` § Step 0.4c) —
never the most expensive rung and never unset. A recorded rung the resolved model does
not support is HONORED and FLAGGED rather than dropped, in the spirit of
`wf-model-budget`'s out-of-pool default: a user's recorded choice disappearing from
the slate it is pre-selected in is the silent discard this project keeps finding. A
recorded value that is not a rung AT ALL cannot be honored — the ladder is the whole
set the harness accepts — so it is reported and the lane falls back to its
recommendation.

WINDOWING. `AskUserQuestion` caps options at four and the full ladder is five, so a
lane offers the FOUR RUNGS NEAREST its recommended rung, always including that rung
and the recorded default, dropping the far end the lane will not reach. A tie drops
the CHEAP end, which is what `audit-setup.md` § Step 0.4c specifies (`low` goes for a
`high`-recommended lane; `max` goes for a `medium`-recommended one). A lane whose
model supports four or fewer rungs offers them all and drops nothing.

There is NO "Other" rung, and this script never emits one. The ladder is the complete
set the harness accepts, so a hand-typed value could only be a rung already offered or
one that does not exist.

The recommendation is a LABEL, never a POSITION — the same rule the model budget
follows, and here for a sharper reason: the two questions render back to back, so a
reader who has just learned that the top of one list is the expensive end must not
have to unlearn it one question later. `(recommended)` is appended in place.

WHAT IT REFUSES: the ladder, the recommendations, and the wording are NEVER read from
`--config`. Only recorded per-lane values are. If the project's `org-config.md`
carries its own `## Effort statics` heading, it is reported as a stale legacy artifact
and read PAST, never clobbered — the project file is the user's
(`org-config.template.md` § Model statics states the never-clobber rule; it holds for
both statics sections).

EXIT CODES: 0 normal (including when a stale embedded section, an unsupported recorded
rung, or an unknown recorded value was reported — each is a finding to surface, not a
failure to abort on); 2 when `--root` is empty, when § Effort statics or § Budget
question wording cannot be found or parsed, when `--models` names a lane that does not
exist, or on an AVAILABILITY CONTRADICTION — a rung named in platform.md that is not
on the ladder, a lane recommended a rung its resolved model does not accept, or a
window that cannot reach the option cap without dropping a protected rung. In each of
those the caller has no trustworthy ladder and must not fall back to reconstructing
one.
"""

import argparse
import os
import re
import sys

# The canonical lane order, owned by org-config.template.md § The four lanes and
# restated in neither budget. The lane KEY is the token both budgets agree on; the
# second field is the object header, the third its prompt.
LANES = [
    ("analytical-lead", "analytical · Lead", "Agents that coordinate"),
    ("analytical-ic", "analytical · IC", "Agents that do the work"),
    ("creative-text", "creative-text", "Writing & copy work"),
    ("creative-visual", "creative-visual", "Graphics & frontend design work"),
    ("code", "code", "Code work"),
]

# AskUserQuestion accepts at most this many objects per call (platform.md § header)...
_OBJECT_CAP = 4
# ...and at most this many options within one object. Aliased rather than restated so
# the number lives in exactly one place in this file (SKILL.md Principle 9a).
_OPTION_CAP = _OBJECT_CAP

# Five lanes overflow one call, so the budget renders as two — the IDENTICAL grouping
# wf-model-budget uses. The validation below refuses a grouping that drops,
# duplicates, or overfills a lane.
CALL_GROUPS = [
    ("CALL A", "structural lanes", ("analytical-lead", "analytical-ic", "code")),
    ("CALL B", "creative lanes", ("creative-text", "creative-visual")),
]

_LANE_KEYS = [k for k, _lbl, _p in LANES]
_LANE_LABEL = {k: lbl for k, lbl, _p in LANES}
_LANE_PROMPT = {k: p for k, _lbl, p in LANES}

# A § Model statics row: | 1 | `<model-id>` | 1M | 128K | ...notes... |
_POOL_ROW_RE = re.compile(r"^\|\s*\d+\s*\|\s*`([^`]+)`\s*\|.*\|.*\|\s*(.*?)\s*\|\s*$")

# The `### Wording: <budget> / CALL <letter>` sub-headings of § Budget question wording.
_WORDING_HEAD_RE = re.compile(r"^###\s+Wording:\s*([A-Za-z-]+)\s*/\s*CALL\s+([A-Z])\s*$")

# Per-model availability, read from platform.md wherever it is stated rather than from
# a hardcoded fact number: a fact renumbered or restated elsewhere in that file is
# still read, and no model ID is written here.
_AVAIL_ALL_RE = re.compile(r"`([A-Za-z][\w.-]*)`\s+accepts\s+[^.\n]*?effort rungs\s*[—-]\s*([^.\n]*)")
_AVAIL_NOT_RE = re.compile(r"`([A-Za-z][\w.-]*)`\s*\(no\s+`(\w+)`\)")
_AVAIL_NONE_RE = re.compile(
    r"`([A-Za-z][\w.-]*)`[^`\n]{0,60}?rejects\s+(?:the\s+)?`?effort`?(?:\s+parameter)?\s+entirely")


def _die(msg, code=2):
    sys.stderr.write("wf-effort-budget: " + msg + "\n")
    sys.exit(code)


def _read(path):
    try:
        with open(path, "r", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            return fh.read()
    except OSError as exc:
        _die("cannot read %s: %s" % (path, exc))


def _validate_grouping():
    """The call grouping must partition the lanes exactly and fit the tool's cap.

    A lane silently missing from both calls is a lane the user is never asked about,
    and the run would pin it to a default nobody chose."""
    grouped = [k for _n, _d, keys in CALL_GROUPS for k in keys]
    if sorted(grouped) != sorted(_LANE_KEYS):
        _die("internal: CALL_GROUPS does not partition LANES (%s vs %s)"
             % (", ".join(sorted(grouped)), ", ".join(sorted(_LANE_KEYS))))
    for name, _desc, keys in CALL_GROUPS:
        if len(keys) > _OBJECT_CAP:
            _die("internal: %s carries %d objects; the cap is %d per call"
                 % (name, len(keys), _OBJECT_CAP))


def default_reference(name):
    """A shipped reference co-located with this script: bin/ and references/ are
    siblings in all three copies (source, runtime, personal install)."""
    here = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
    return os.path.normpath(os.path.join(here, "..", "references", name))


def _section(text, heading_re):
    """The body between a heading matching heading_re and the next `## `."""
    out, capturing = [], False
    for line in text.splitlines():
        if capturing:
            if line.startswith("## "):
                break
            out.append(line)
        elif heading_re.match(line):
            capturing = True
    return "\n".join(out) if capturing else None


def _lane_key(label):
    """Normalise a canonical lane label to its key: `analytical · Lead` →
    `analytical-lead`. The middot, the spaces, and the capitals are presentation."""
    return re.sub(r"[^a-z0-9]+", "-", label.strip().lower()).strip("-")


def _rec_lanes(text):
    """Every lane a `**Recommended for <lane>**` annotation on this text names.

    Derived from the lane KEYS rather than restating five phrases: `analytical-lead`
    matches "Recommended for analytical Lead". The trailing `(?![\\w-])` keeps the two
    creative lanes apart — without it a `creative-text` pattern would swallow
    `creative-visual`'s annotation. One row may carry several annotations (since
    2026-09-02 the top pool row is recommended for both `code` and `creative-visual`),
    so this returns all of them, in canonical lane order, and an empty list when the
    text carries none. Read exactly the way wf-model-budget reads it."""
    found = []
    for key in _LANE_KEYS:
        pat = r"Recommended for " + key.replace("-", "[ -]") + r"(?![\w-])"
        if re.search(pat, text, re.I):
            found.append(key)
    return found


# --- template: ladder, recommendations, fallback models, wording -----------------

def _effort_body(template_text):
    body = _section(template_text, re.compile(r"^##\s+Effort statics"))
    if body is None:
        _die("template has no '## Effort statics' section: cannot derive the ladder")
    return body


def parse_ladder(template_text):
    """The rungs in cost order, most expensive first, from § Effort statics."""
    body = _effort_body(template_text)
    m = re.search(r"The rungs are\s+([^(\n]*)", body)
    rungs = [t.strip() for t in re.findall(r"`([^`]+)`", m.group(1))] if m else []
    rungs = [r for r in rungs if re.match(r"^[a-z]+$", r)]
    if len(rungs) < 2:
        _die("'## Effort statics' present but no rung ladder parsed: the "
             "'The rungs are `...`' line changed shape")
    if len(set(rungs)) != len(rungs):
        _die("the rung ladder repeats a rung (%s): the cost order is ambiguous"
             % ", ".join(rungs))
    return rungs


def parse_rung_recommendations(template_text, ladder):
    """{lane_key: rung} from § Effort statics' recommendation table."""
    body = _effort_body(template_text)
    rec = {}
    for cells in _rows(body):
        if len(cells) < 2:
            continue
        lane = _lane_key(re.sub(r"`", "", cells[0]))
        if lane not in _LANE_KEYS:
            continue
        m = re.search(r"`([^`]+)`", cells[1])
        rung = (m.group(1) if m else cells[1]).strip()
        if rung not in ladder:
            _die("lane '%s' is recommended effort '%s', which is not a rung on the "
                 "ladder (%s): the recommendation and the ladder disagree"
                 % (lane, rung, ", ".join(ladder)))
        rec[lane] = rung
    if not rec:
        _die("no per-lane effort recommendation parsed from '## Effort statics': the "
             "recommendation table changed shape")
    return rec


def parse_model_recommendations(template_text):
    """{lane_key: model_id} from § Model statics — the availability FALLBACK only.

    Read exactly the way wf-model-budget reads it: the per-lane annotation sits in a
    pool row's Notes cell, or, for the one sanctioned out-of-pool recommendation, on a
    prose line beside a backticked ID that is not a pool row."""
    body = _section(template_text, re.compile(r"^##\s+Model statics"))
    if body is None:
        _die("template has no '## Model statics' section: a lane with no supplied or "
             "recorded model has no fallback to compute rung availability from")
    pool, rec = [], {}
    for line in body.splitlines():
        m = _POOL_ROW_RE.match(line)
        if m:
            pool.append(m.group(1).strip())
    for line in body.splitlines():
        lanes = _rec_lanes(line)
        if not lanes:
            continue
        m = _POOL_ROW_RE.match(line)
        if m:
            for lane in lanes:
                rec[lane] = m.group(1).strip()
            continue
        outside = [t.strip() for t in re.findall(r"`([^`]+)`", line)
                   if t.strip() and t.strip() not in pool]
        if outside:
            for lane in lanes:
                rec.setdefault(lane, outside[0])
    if not rec:
        _die("no lane is annotated 'Recommended for <lane>' in '## Model statics': "
             "the availability fallback has no source")
    return rec


def parse_wording(template_text):
    """{(budget, call_letter): (header_line, [body_lines])} from § Budget question
    wording — the ONE home of the four calls' user-facing copy.

    The blockquote's first line is the question header and every line after it is the
    body, blank lines included."""
    body = _section(template_text, re.compile(r"^##\s+Budget question wording"))
    if body is None:
        _die("template has no '## Budget question wording' section: the caller would "
             "reconstruct the question text by hand, which is the drift this emitter "
             "exists to end")
    found, key, quoted = {}, None, []

    def _close():
        if key and quoted:
            found[key] = (quoted[0], quoted[1:])

    for line in body.splitlines():
        m = _WORDING_HEAD_RE.match(line)
        if m:
            _close()
            key, quoted = (m.group(1).strip().lower(), m.group(2).strip().upper()), []
        elif line.startswith(">") and key:
            quoted.append(line[1:].lstrip(" ") if line[1:2] == " " else line[1:])
        elif line.strip() and key and quoted:
            _close()
            key, quoted = None, []
    _close()
    return found


def wording_for(wording, budget, call_name):
    letter = call_name.split()[-1]
    got = wording.get((budget, letter))
    if got is None:
        _die("no wording block for '%s / %s' in '## Budget question wording': every "
             "call renders header, body, and options together or the caller retypes "
             "the half that is missing" % (budget, call_name))
    return got


def _rows(text):
    """Cell lists for every markdown table row in text."""
    for line in text.splitlines():
        if not line.lstrip().startswith("|"):
            continue
        yield [c.strip() for c in line.strip().strip("|").split("|")]


# --- platform.md: per-model rung availability ------------------------------------

def parse_availability(platform_text, ladder):
    """{model_id: set(rungs) or None} — None meaning the model REJECTS effort.

    Anti-vacuity: a parse that finds NO per-model statement is refused rather than
    treated as "everything supports everything". Silently widening every ladder is
    exactly the failure a prose-only rule produces, and it would render an effort
    object for a model that rejects the parameter."""
    avail, seen = {}, 0
    for m in _AVAIL_ALL_RE.finditer(platform_text):
        rungs = [t.strip() for t in re.findall(r"`([^`]+)`", m.group(2))]
        rungs = [r for r in rungs if re.match(r"^[a-z]+$", r)]
        if not rungs:
            continue
        bad = [r for r in rungs if r not in ladder]
        if bad:
            _die("availability contradiction: platform.md says '%s' accepts rung(s) "
                 "%s, which are not on the ladder (%s)"
                 % (m.group(1), ", ".join(bad), ", ".join(ladder)))
        avail[m.group(1)] = set(rungs)
        seen += 1
    for m in _AVAIL_NOT_RE.finditer(platform_text):
        model, rung = m.group(1), m.group(2)
        if rung not in ladder:
            _die("availability contradiction: platform.md excludes rung '%s' from "
                 "'%s', and '%s' is not on the ladder (%s)"
                 % (rung, model, rung, ", ".join(ladder)))
        base = avail.get(model)
        avail[model] = (set(ladder) if base is None else set(base)) - {rung}
        seen += 1
    for m in _AVAIL_NONE_RE.finditer(platform_text):
        avail[m.group(1)] = None
        seen += 1
    if not seen:
        _die("no per-model effort availability parsed from platform.md: facts 12b/12c "
             "state which models accept which rungs, and a ladder derived without them "
             "would offer every rung to every model — including one that rejects effort")
    return avail


def supported_rungs(avail, model, ladder):
    """The rungs a model accepts. A model platform.md says nothing about supports the
    whole ladder (fact 12b: availability depends on the model, and the exceptions are
    the documented ones). Returns None when the model rejects effort entirely."""
    if model in avail:
        return avail[model]
    return set(ladder)


# --- project config (re-audit values only; NEVER the ladder) ---------------------

def _cell_value(cells, idx):
    if len(cells) <= idx:
        return None
    raw = re.sub(r"[`*]", "", cells[idx]).strip()
    return raw or None


def parse_config(config_text):
    """({lane: model}, {lane: rung}) recorded in a project's org-config.md.

    Best-effort: a lane that cannot be found simply has no recorded value. A config
    written before the creative lane split records one `Creative model` / `Creative
    effort` row and no visual row; that row is the recorded TEXT lane, and reading it
    as nothing would silently discard a choice the user made."""
    models, efforts = {}, {}

    def _take(lane, cells, model_idx, effort_idx):
        if lane in models and lane in efforts:
            return
        if model_idx is not None:
            m = re.search(r"`([^`]+)`", cells[model_idx]) if len(cells) > model_idx else None
            if m and lane not in models:
                models[lane] = m.group(1).strip()
        if effort_idx is not None:
            val = _cell_value(cells, effort_idx)
            if val and re.match(r"^[A-Za-z]+$", val) and lane not in efforts:
                efforts[lane] = val.lower()

    labels = [
        (re.compile(r"^Lead\b", re.I), "analytical-lead", 1, 2),
        (re.compile(r"^IC\b", re.I), "analytical-ic", 1, 2),
        (re.compile(r"^Creative-text model\b", re.I), "creative-text", 1, None),
        (re.compile(r"^Creative-text effort\b", re.I), "creative-text", None, 1),
        (re.compile(r"^Creative-visual model\b", re.I), "creative-visual", 1, None),
        (re.compile(r"^Creative-visual effort\b", re.I), "creative-visual", None, 1),
        (re.compile(r"^Code model\b", re.I), "code", 1, None),
        (re.compile(r"^Code effort\b", re.I), "code", None, 1),
        # Pre-split labels, read last so a current row always wins.
        (re.compile(r"^Creative model\b", re.I), "creative-text", 1, None),
        (re.compile(r"^Creative effort\b", re.I), "creative-text", None, 1),
    ]
    rows = list(_rows(config_text))
    for pat, lane, mi, ei in labels:
        for cells in rows:
            if cells and pat.search(cells[0]):
                _take(lane, cells, mi, ei)
    return models, efforts


def config_has_stale_statics(config_text):
    return bool(re.search(r"^##\s+Effort statics", config_text, re.M))


# --- windowing -------------------------------------------------------------------

def window(ladder, supported, rec_rung, recorded_rung, lane_key):
    """The rungs THIS lane offers, in cost order, and the ones it gave up.

    The four nearest the recommended rung, always including that rung and the recorded
    default, dropping the far end the lane will not reach. A tie drops the CHEAP end
    (`audit-setup.md` § Step 0.4c: `low` goes for a `high`-recommended lane). A lane
    whose model supports four or fewer rungs offers them all."""
    protected = {r for r in (rec_rung, recorded_rung) if r}
    rungs = [r for r in ladder if r in supported or r == recorded_rung]
    dropped = []
    while len(rungs) > _OPTION_CAP:
        i_rec = rungs.index(rec_rung) if rec_rung in rungs else 0
        d_head, d_tail = i_rec, len(rungs) - 1 - i_rec
        head_free, tail_free = rungs[0] not in protected, rungs[-1] not in protected
        if not head_free and not tail_free:
            _die("availability contradiction: lane '%s' cannot fit the %d-option cap "
                 "— the recommended rung '%s' and the recorded rung '%s' sit at "
                 "opposite ends of a %d-rung ladder, and neither may be dropped"
                 % (lane_key, _OPTION_CAP, rec_rung, recorded_rung, len(rungs)))
        if head_free and (not tail_free or d_head > d_tail):
            dropped.append(rungs.pop(0))
        else:
            dropped.append(rungs.pop())
    return rungs, dropped


# --- emission --------------------------------------------------------------------

def _lane_block(lane_key, ladder, rec_rungs, model, model_src, supported, recorded):
    """One AskUserQuestion object, rendered — or the refusal to render one."""
    out = ["LANE %s  (object: \"%s\")" % (_LANE_LABEL[lane_key], _LANE_PROMPT[lane_key])]
    out.append("  model: %s  [%s]" % (model, model_src))
    if supported is None:
        out.append("  !! NO EFFORT OBJECT: %s rejects the effort parameter entirely "
                   "(platform.md). Render NO object for this lane — not a blank one, "
                   "and not a rung it will refuse." % model)
        out.append("")
        return out, False

    rec_rung = rec_rungs.get(lane_key)
    if rec_rung is None:
        _die("no rung is marked recommended for lane '%s' in the template's "
             "§ Effort statics recommendation table" % lane_key)
    if rec_rung not in supported:
        _die("availability contradiction: lane '%s' is recommended effort '%s', which "
             "its model '%s' does not accept (accepts: %s). The recommendation is the "
             "forced first-run default and cannot be offered"
             % (lane_key, rec_rung, model, ", ".join(r for r in ladder if r in supported)))

    unknown = recorded is not None and recorded not in ladder
    honored = recorded if (recorded and not unknown) else None
    default = honored or rec_rung
    rungs, dropped = window(ladder, supported, rec_rung, honored, lane_key)
    for rung in rungs:
        marks = []
        if rung == rec_rung:
            marks.append("(recommended)")
        if rung == default:
            marks.append("[pre-selected]")
        out.append("  - %s%s" % (rung, ("  " + " ".join(marks)) if marks else ""))
    if dropped:
        out.append("  dropped to fit the %d-option cap (farthest from the "
                   "recommendation): %s" % (_OPTION_CAP, ", ".join(dropped)))
    out.append("  no \"Other\" rung — the ladder is the whole set the harness accepts")
    if honored and honored not in supported:
        out.append("    HONORED-UNSUPPORTED: %s is the recorded rung and stays "
                   "pre-selected, but platform.md does not list it for %s. Honored, "
                   "flagged, never silently dropped — a recorded choice vanishing "
                   "from the slate it is pre-selected in is a silent discard."
                   % (honored, model))
    if unknown:
        out.append("    IGNORED-UNKNOWN-RUNG: this lane records '%s', which is not a "
                   "rung on the ladder (%s). There is no \"Other\" rung to honor it "
                   "with, so the lane falls back to its recommended rung."
                   % (recorded, ", ".join(ladder)))
    out.append("  default source: %s"
               % ("recorded (re-audit)" if honored else "recommended default (first run)"))
    out.append("")
    return out, True


def emit(ladder, rec_rungs, models, model_srcs, avail, recorded_efforts, wording,
         stale, template_path, platform_path):
    out = ["WF-EFFORT-BUDGET  (Step 0.4c/0.4d option set — render verbatim, do not reorder)",
           "source: %s § Effort statics" % template_path,
           "wording source: %s § Budget question wording" % template_path,
           "availability source: %s (per-model rungs; DOCUMENTED, unverified)" % platform_path,
           "ladder (cost order, most expensive first): " + ", ".join(ladder),
           "lanes: %d, rendered as %d AskUserQuestion calls (cap: %d objects per call)"
           % (len(LANES), len(CALL_GROUPS), _OBJECT_CAP),
           ""]
    for call_name, call_desc, keys in CALL_GROUPS:
        ordered = [k for k in _LANE_KEYS if k in keys]
        blocks, rendered = [], []
        for lane_key in ordered:
            model = models[lane_key]
            block, has_object = _lane_block(
                lane_key, ladder, rec_rungs, model, model_srcs[lane_key],
                supported_rungs(avail, model, ladder), recorded_efforts.get(lane_key))
            blocks.extend(block)
            if has_object:
                rendered.append(lane_key)
        silent = len(ordered) - len(rendered)
        out.append("%s  (%s — %d objects: %s%s)"
                   % (call_name, call_desc, len(rendered),
                      ", ".join(_LANE_LABEL[k] for k in rendered) or "none",
                      ("; %d lane%s no effort object"
                       % (silent, " renders" if silent == 1 else "s render")) if silent else ""))
        header, body = wording_for(wording, "effort", call_name)
        out.append("QUESTION-HEADER-BEGIN")
        out.append(header)
        out.append("QUESTION-HEADER-END")
        out.append("QUESTION-BODY-BEGIN")
        out.extend(body)
        out.append("QUESTION-BODY-END")
        out.append("")
        out.extend(blocks)
    if stale:
        out.append("STALE-ARTIFACT: the project's org-config.md carries a '## Effort statics' "
                   "heading. The ladder was read from the template, never from that copy. "
                   "Report it as a stale legacy artifact; never rewrite or delete it "
                   "(org-config.template.md § Model statics — the never-clobber rule holds).")
    else:
        out.append("stale embedded '## Effort statics' in project config: none")
    return "\n".join(out)


def parse_models_flag(raw):
    """`--models lane=model,...`. An unknown lane is refused, never ignored: a
    misspelled lane would otherwise fall back to the recommended model and window a
    ladder the caller did not ask for, silently."""
    supplied = {}
    for item in (raw or "").split(","):
        item = item.strip()
        if not item:
            continue
        if "=" not in item:
            _die("--models expects lane=model pairs; got %r" % item)
        lane, model = item.split("=", 1)
        key = _lane_key(lane)
        if key not in _LANE_KEYS:
            _die("--models names lane %r, which is not a budget lane. The five are: %s"
                 % (lane.strip(), ", ".join(_LANE_KEYS)))
        if not model.strip():
            _die("--models gives lane %r an empty model" % lane.strip())
        supplied[key] = model.strip()
    if raw is not None and not supplied:
        _die("--models was passed but named no lane")
    return supplied


def main(argv=None):
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="wf-effort-budget",
        description="Emit the effort budget's option set and wording from the shipped template.",
    )
    ap.add_argument("--root", default=".",
                    help="base for resolving relative --template/--platform/--config")
    ap.add_argument("--template", default=None,
                    help="path to org-config.template.md (default: co-located references/ copy)")
    ap.add_argument("--platform", default=None,
                    help="path to platform.md (default: co-located references/ copy)")
    ap.add_argument("--config", default=None,
                    help="path to the project's org-config.md (re-audit values + stale-section check)")
    ap.add_argument("--models", default=None,
                    help="lane=model,... — the models the model budget just resolved; "
                         "outranks --config, which outranks the recommended model")
    args = ap.parse_args(argv)

    # AN EMPTY --root IS A CALLER ERROR, NEVER A SILENT RETARGET TO CWD.
    # `${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}` is UNSET in the Bash tool — measured 2026-08-04 on
    # 2.1.221 — so every shipped `--root "${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}"` block expands to
    # `--root ""`. `os.path.abspath("")` is the CWD, a real directory, so an
    # is-it-a-directory guard passes and the emitter would resolve its template
    # against a tree nobody named — deriving the ladder, or failing about the wrong
    # file entirely. Refuse it and name the empty argument.
    _validate_grouping()
    if not (args.root or "").strip():
        _die("--root is empty. ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR} is unset outside a hook; "
             "pass an explicit path.")

    def _resolve(p):
        return p if os.path.isabs(p) else os.path.join(args.root, p)

    template_path = (_resolve(args.template) if args.template
                     else default_reference("org-config.template.md"))
    platform_path = (_resolve(args.platform) if args.platform
                     else default_reference("platform.md"))
    template_text = _read(template_path)
    ladder = parse_ladder(template_text)
    rec_rungs = parse_rung_recommendations(template_text, ladder)
    rec_models = parse_model_recommendations(template_text)
    wording = parse_wording(template_text)
    avail = parse_availability(_read(platform_path), ladder)

    supplied = parse_models_flag(args.models) if args.models is not None else {}
    recorded_models, recorded_efforts, stale = {}, {}, False
    config_path = _resolve(args.config) if args.config else None
    if config_path and os.path.exists(config_path):
        config_text = _read(config_path)
        recorded_models, recorded_efforts = parse_config(config_text)
        stale = config_has_stale_statics(config_text)

    models, model_srcs = {}, {}
    for key in _LANE_KEYS:
        if key in supplied:
            models[key], model_srcs[key] = supplied[key], "supplied (--models)"
        elif key in recorded_models:
            models[key], model_srcs[key] = recorded_models[key], "recorded (re-audit)"
        elif key in rec_models:
            models[key], model_srcs[key] = rec_models[key], "recommended model (fallback)"
        else:
            _die("lane '%s' has no model: none supplied by --models, none recorded in "
                 "--config, and none recommended in the template's § Model statics. "
                 "Without a model there is no rung availability to window" % key)

    sys.stdout.write(emit(ladder, rec_rungs, models, model_srcs, avail, recorded_efforts,
                          wording, stale, template_path, platform_path) + "\n")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
